===== Resolve unstable WiFi (slow-downs and disconnections of all clients) =====

At least up to openwrt version 23.05 you may get WiFi slow-downs and a total WiFi lockdown, with disconnects of most or all clients in a few minutes, until you reboot or perform a "/sbin/wifi down" followed by "/sbin/wifi up". This seems to happen especially with many clients connected and/or heavy traffic. To avoid this problem add this line:
<code>
	option ldpc '0'
</code>
to file "**/etc/config/wireless**", in the 2.4GHz radio section, usually the one that begins with this line:
<code>
 "config wifi-device 'radio0'
</code>
This solution was found in [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/archer-c7-2-4-ghz-wireless-dies-in-24-48-hours/44163/260|this thread]] on the forum.

